# Backup/snapshot copies an agent leaves behind before editing a Wine source file (a defensive
# "save the original before I touch it" copy, e.g. "bcrypt_main.c.pre_capiexport",
# "cert.c.bak.wbsdiag", "device.c.orig", "protectdata.c.pristine", "loader.c.v12") are working
# notes, never part of the actual patch. Committed alongside real fixes, they've repeatedly
# polluted the dashboard's Patches tab: one commit's real ~2-file fix showed as +120,828 lines
# across 67 files because 60+ of these snapshot copies rode along in the same commit. Keep them
# out of git entirely so this can't recur -- see /root/wbs/sim/state.py's _is_artifact_path() /
# _ARTIFACT_SEGMENT_RE for the dashboard-side filter this list is meant to make unnecessary
# going forward (that filter stays too, for the already-committed history it can't rewrite).
#
# Patterns are broad substring matches (verified against the full tracked tree with zero
# collisions against real Wine filenames -- no legitimate source file has ".pre"/".bak"/".clean"/
# ".orig" as a substring of its name).
*.clean*
*.bak*
*.pre*
*.orig*
*.winorig
*.etwbak
*.pristine
*.baseline*
*.v[0-9]*
*.rej
*~
